[PHASE 4: FILE SYSTEM OWNERSHIP & LEAST-PRIVILEGE PERMISSION HARDENING]
(Sprint 3 - Advanced Operations: chmod / chown Configuration)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ cd "$APP_ROOT"

# Set recursive user and group ownership without error suppression
$ chown -R mw851:sprints_ops "$APP_ROOT"
Applied ownership 'mw851:sprints_ops' recursively to application tree.

# 1. Directory permissions: 750 (rwxr-x---)
# Owner full access; sprints_ops group read/execute/traverse; others no access
$ find "$APP_ROOT" -type d -exec chmod 750 {} +

# 2. Executable scripts and Python code: 750 (rwxr-x---)
$ find "$APP_ROOT/code" -type f -name "*.py" -exec chmod 750 {} +
$ find "$APP_ROOT/scripts" -type f -name "*.sh" -exec chmod 750 {} +

# 3. Relational database and CSV data files: 660 (rw-rw----)
# Ensures group members have read/write access without requiring root/sudo
$ find "$APP_ROOT/data" -type f -exec chmod 660 {} +

# 4. Operational Activity Logs: 660 (rw-rw----)
$ find "$APP_ROOT/logs" -type f -exec chmod 660 {} +

# 5. Documentation & Markdown specifications: 640 (rw-r-----)
$ find "$APP_ROOT/docs" -type f -exec chmod 640 {} +
$ find "$APP_ROOT" -maxdepth 1 -type f -name "*.md" -exec chmod 640 {} +

